mpensation of $656 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["McEwen Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $925M market cap on $198M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -15% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 9% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 8% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 295% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.9455798479087454},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (MUX) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_MUX_Volatility_110226032202_1793650922.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793650922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"McEwen Mining (TSE:MUX) Reaches New 1-Year Low \u2013 Here\u2019s Why","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/24/mcewen-mining-tsemux-reaches-new-1-year-low-heres-why.html","date":"2026-10-24","timestamp":1792852880.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"McEwen Inc. $MUX Stake Increased by U S Global Investors Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/23/mcewen-inc-mux-stake-increased-by-u-s-global-investors-inc.html","date":"2026-10-23","timestamp":1792750645.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Cabot Q4 Earnings Beat on Performance Chemicals Strength","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025248/cabot-q4-earnings-beat-on-performance-chemicals-strength?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_article-3025248","date":"2026-1